osed_loop_lab_safety_replay","mathematical_strategy_atlas_hypothesis_scorer","navigation_hologram_route_plane","pattern_assimilation_step","pattern_binding_contract","proof_diagnostic_evidence_spine","provider_context_recipe_budget_policy","public_reveal_walkthrough","research_replication_rubric_artifact_replay","ring2_premise_retrieval_precision_recall_harness","routing_anti_patterns_registry","semantic_singleflight_dedup_runtime","spatial_world_model_counterfactual_simulation_replay","tactic_portfolio_availability_probe","target_shape_tactic_routing_gate","undeclared_library_prior_symbol_classifier","verifier_lab_execution_spine","verifier_lab_kernel","world_model_projection_drift_control_room"],"exposed_count":0,"exposure":[],"failure_modes":[],"id":"P-1","kind":"principle","plain":"Treat a fixture label, a declared verdict, a route status, a count or a line of public copy as a statement to check. Recompute the verdict from the lower-level evidence, and keep a negative fixture with a deliberately wrong label, so that a check which only repeats labels fails.","principles":[],"reader":{"analogy":{"boundary":"The marking picture covers recomputation and the planted wrong answer only; a real check may read many more kinds of evidence than one exam paper.","maps":[{"analogy":"the exam paper itself, worked from scratch","doctrine":"the evidence underneath the verdict"},{"analogy":"working the answer out again instead of copying the key","doctrine":"recomputing the verdict from the evidence"},{"analogy":"the planted wrong answer the marking must catch","doctrine":"the negative test case the checker must reject"}],"text":"A teacher marks an exam by working each answer out from scratch instead of copying the answer key, and slips in a paper with a planted wrong answer to confirm the marking catches it."},"basis":"authored_reader_enrichment","counterexample":"A summary copies a component's self-reported \"passed\" onto a status board without recomputing it and without any test case that could fail.","does_not_prove":"Recomputing one verdict shows that this verdict follows from its evidence, and says nothing about verdicts nobody recomputed.","enforced_in_component_ids":["agent_sabotage_scheming_monitor_replay","agent_benchmark_integrity_anti_gaming_replay"],"example":{"component_ids":["agent_benchmark_integrity_anti_gaming_replay"],"text":"The benchmark-integrity replay recomputes a score from the recorded run instead of trusting the reported number, and keeps known gaming attempts as test cases that the replay must catch."},"governs":"Whether a stated result may be used as evidence.","plain":"Trust a result only after working it out again from the underlying evidence, and keep a deliberately wrong test case that the check has to reject.","potential_misread":"That checking a result once makes it safe for good, when the check only covers that result against that test.","refuses":"Repeating a declared verdict, label or count as if it had been checked.","requires":"Recomputing the verdict from lower-level evidence, and a negative test case that the checker rejects.","source_ref":"core/doctrine_enrichment.json","why_it_matters":"It stops a label saying 'passed' from being copied from report to report when nobody has worked out whether it was true."},"rests_on":["AX-1"],"source_ref":"PRINCIPLES.md::P-1","statement":"Grounding: AX-1.\nObligation grounding: AX-1.O1.certificate_exists, AX-1.O2.checker_accepts, AX-1.O3.claim_ceiling, AX-1.O4.bare_assertion_bottom.\n\nTreat a fixture label, a declared verdict, a route status, a count or a line of\npublic copy as a statement to check. Recompute the verdict from the lower-level\nevidence, and keep a negative fixture with a deliberately wrong label, so that a\ncheck which only repeats labels fails.","statement_sha256":"60c6c9925f320caa805ac7d24c7a546283c0cd3a35b73b641b536e541243b5e4","title":"Recompute, do not echo","violates":[]},"schema_version":"plectis_component_http_v1","snapshot_revision":"45be1deb333ad57cd9ae093229455d0a52d3bf23a9064cde09f1a6e16f4c7044"}